---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import ScreencastRedactor from '@/components/tools/redact/screencast/ScreencastRedactor.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="redact-screen-recording" width="wide">
  <ScreencastRedactor client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to redact a screen recording</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Drop a screen recording: MP4, MOV or WebM.</li>
      <li>Press Read the recording. The tool reads the screen each time it changes and lists every email, name, key and number it finds, with the times it is on screen.</li>
      <li>Switch off an item to keep it visible. Choose types, add words to the always-hide list, and switch faces on or off.</li>
      <li>Pause on a frame and press Add a box to cover anything else. Set the time span of each box in the list.</li>
      <li>Play the preview, then download the video.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Frames are taken three times a second. When the screen has changed, the frame is read with the OCR engine (about 7 MB),
      and the text is checked by pattern rules for emails, phone numbers, keys and tokens and by a small language model (21 MB)
      for names and places. A face detector (under 1 MB) looks at every frame, and a tracker follows each face. The models run on
      a 15 MB runtime. These files download once from this site. The video is decoded and encoded by your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      A box starts one frame before the text was read and stays until a later reading no longer finds the text there, so the
      moment the screen changes is covered by both the old and the new boxes.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>
      Open your browser's developer tools, select the Network tab and run the tool. You see the engine and models load from
      this site the first time, and no request after that.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Fast scrolling can show text between two readings for a fraction of a second. Play the preview and add boxes where you see text.</li>
      <li>Small or low-contrast text can be missed by the OCR. Record at full resolution if you can.</li>
      <li>A recording with much change takes longer, because more frames are read. A minute of busy screen takes a few minutes.</li>
      <li>The result is H.264 MP4 when the browser can encode it, otherwise WebM.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
